<title>UK: Tesco, ASDA up as UBS repeats &quot;buy&quot;.</title>
<headline>Tesco, ASDA up as UBS repeats &quot;buy&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British retailers Tesco Plc and ASDA Group Plc climbed on Wednesday as analysts at UBS repeated a &quot;buy&quot; recommendation on the stocks, dealers said.</p>
<p>Tesco was up five pence at 361-1/2 by 1250 GMT while ASDA gained 1-1/4p to 121-1/4.</p>
<p>Analysts at UBS said they had issued a major piece of research on Wednesday on the outlook for the Tesco and ASDA in 1997, which restated their positive stance on the two stocks.  </p>
<p>Other retailers also firmed -- Safeway was up 4-1/2p at 384 and Sainsbury gained a penny to 325.</p>
<p>Safeway declined to comment on reports that it was mulling a bid for Fitzwilton Plc's Wellworth unit, which operates a chain of supermarkets in Northern Ireland.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
